# L §8 Refusals outrank holes (tally 2.1.7 R2, issue #141; #104): a refusal is the instance's status. A decision
# whose key's `where` is refused (February: a division by zero) is kept, runs at its point as any instance does, its
# leg's place read there (it reads bal(box)), and refuses that place, box, from its day; March's instance, whose place
# reads the refused box, refuses every place (L §8.4; E §4.2 step 3). The engine's bytes. 2.1.6's refcore dropped
# February's instance: (100.00 PLN, 3.00 PLN) on 20 February.
=== m.tally
model g5_dec_where_place
  tally 2
  on 2026-02-15
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-03-31

source fixture "T's fixture for S's kernel tests (invented values)"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

index month = month 2026-01..2026-03

place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..

place box: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..

place world: outside lives 2026-01-01..

input dec_dom: int

input fee_amt: money PLN

input small_put: money PLN

input divisor[m in month]: num

move split[m in month where 1 / divisor[m] > 0]: transfers
  on day_of(m, dec_dom)
  at start_of(m)
  reads box
  leg cash from world to (if bal(box) > fee_amt then konto else box) amount fee_amt

ask q_bal: bal(konto, d), bal(box, d) for d in [2026-01-20, 2026-02-19, 2026-02-20, 2026-03-20] law cut

version facts
  cite fixture
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  dec_dom = 20 "the decision's day of the month"
  fee_amt = 3.00 "a fee"
  small_put = 1.00 "a small amount"
  divisor[2026-01] = 1 "answered"
  divisor[2026-02] = 0 "a division by zero, refused"
  divisor[2026-03] = 2 "answered, but after February's refusal"

version openings
  cite fixture
  governs always
  known 2025-12-31
  opening[konto] = 100 at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[box] = 0 at 2026-01-01 start
=== expect
q_bal (d = 2026-01-20): (100.00 PLN, 3.00 PLN)
...
q_bal (d = 2026-02-19): (100.00 PLN, 3.00 PLN)
...
q_bal (d = 2026-02-20): (100.00 PLN, refused: RUN-DIV division by zero)
...
q_bal (d = 2026-03-20): (refused: RUN-DIV division by zero, refused: RUN-DIV division by zero)
...
warning: WARN-UNREAD input small_put is read by nothing
